          'The three-rebuttal rule is a practical constraint that forces prioritisation. You cannot pre-build credible responses to every possible attack, and attempting to do so produces a document that no one reads. Instead, identify the three attacks that are most likely to land, most likely to damage the campaign if they go unanswered, and most likely to be deployed by your most sophisticated opponents. Write a complete rebuttal for each — a rebuttal being not just a denial but a positive counter-argument that redirects the conversation toward terrain that favours your campaign.',
