          'The second is the journalist test: expose the message house to an experienced political journalist and ask them to find the story in it. Not the story you want them to find — the story they would actually write. Journalists are trained to find inconsistency, to identify claims that cannot be evidenced, and to ask the question that the campaign has avoided answering. If the house fails the journalist test, you have a communications liability, not an asset.',
